REAL HTTP SERVICE (the web-real trigger)
  app.php (COPYed to /var/www/html/index.php) is served by Apache mod_php at the document root:
    GET  /            -> {"status":"ok","phpspreadsheet":"<ver>","php":"8.2.x"}   (health, no lib call)
    POST /  path=<u>  -> app calls the UNMODIFIED Reader\Csv::load($u) and returns
                         {"path","surfaced","error"}.  `surfaced` = loaded row 1; `error` = the
                         library's own exception. The reader load path runs
                         Csv::load -> BaseReader::openFile -> File::assertFile -> File::prohibitWrappers.
  No in-process library call; no source-lift. The version's OWN prohibitWrappers() decides whether the
  phar:// wrapper reaches the loader. Ports: v0=127.0.0.1:38080, v1=38081, v2=38082 (container :80).
  The retired in-process harness.php (docker compose exec) is NOT referenced by compose/oracle/case.json.

SINK EVOLUTION (src/PhpSpreadsheet/Shared/File.php::prohibitWrappers, verbatim from git tags)
  V0 1.30.2 : prohibitWrappers() ABSENT (no wrapper guard on the load path).
  V1 1.30.3 : (CVE-2026-34084 fix)
        $scheme = parse_url($filename, PHP_URL_SCHEME);
        if (is_string($scheme) && strlen($scheme) > 1) { throw ... "Stream wrappers are not permitted..."; }
  V2 1.30.5 : (CVE-2026-45034 fix)
        if (Preg::IsMatch('~^phar://~i', $filename) || ... ) { throw ... "Disallowed stream wrapper..."; }

PARSE_URL BYPASS (confirmed at runtime; app chdir('/') so `phar://work/...` resolves to /work)
  ORIGINAL (seed)   url = phar://work/flag.phar/sheet.csv    parse_url(PHP_URL_SCHEME) => 'phar' (len 4 > 1)
  RESIDUAL (bypass) url = phar:///work/flag.phar/sheet.csv   parse_url(PHP_URL_SCHEME) => false (3 slashes)
  Both address the SAME archive /work/flag.phar; they differ only in the parse_url quirk the 1.30.3 guard
  depends on. Matches the advisory's own two example strings.

